/*
Problem: Maximize the Confusion of an Exam (LC 2024)
Topic: Sliding Window

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

A valid window is one where we can make
all characters the same by changing at
most k characters.

Count:

T = number of 'T'

F = number of 'F'

The minimum of these two counts is the
number of characters that must be flipped.

If:

min(T, F) <= k

the window is valid.

Otherwise, shrink the window.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. Expand the window.

2. Update count of T or F.

3. While min(T, F) > k,
   shrink the window from the left.

4. Update the maximum valid window size.

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

answerKey = "TTFT"

k = 1

Window:

TTFT

T = 3

F = 1

Need to flip only one F.

Valid window length = 4.

Answer = 4

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

To make every character identical,
we only need to flip whichever
character occurs less frequently.

Hence,

Required flips = min(T, F).

As long as this value is at most k,
the window is valid.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n)

Each character enters and leaves the
window at most once.

Space : O(1)

Only two counters are used.

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

Sliding Window + Frequency Count
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int maxConsecutiveAnswers(string answerKey, int k) {

        int st = 0;
        int maxWindow = 0;

        int t = 0;
        int f = 0;

        for (int end = 0; end < answerKey.size(); end++) {

            // Expand window
            if (answerKey[end] == 'T')
                t++;
            else
                f++;

            // Shrink until window becomes valid
            while (min(t, f) > k) {

                if (answerKey[st] == 'T')
                    t--;
                else
                    f--;

                st++;
            }

            maxWindow = max(maxWindow, end - st + 1);
        }

        return maxWindow;
    }
};
